# A gallery-and-viaduct sprint. All structures follow the same driving surface.
name "Stone Gallery"
description "Alternate cool mountain galleries and open viaducts along an undulating stone ridge."
width 12

# Negative world height is valid: terrain follows the course's lowest edge.
# Heading 70 sends this route eastward; height zero has no special ground role.
start 90 -24 -140 70
straight 160 rise 5

# A persistent kind covers every following straight and curve until changed.
kind tunnel
straight 90 rise 7
left 15 radius 100 rise 1 bank 12
left 35 radius 100 rise 3
left 15 radius 100 rise 1 bank 0
straight 70 rise 3
kind road
straight 75 rise 2
checkpoint

# The same persistent-kind pattern builds a viaduct with a curved middle.
width 13
kind bridge
straight 100 rise 12
right 15 radius 100 rise 1 bank -12
right 45 radius 100 rise 4
right 15 radius 100 rise 1 bank 0
straight 70 rise -2
kind road
straight 100 rise -6
checkpoint

# A per-command override makes only this bend a tunnel. The next straight
# returns to the persistent road kind without needing another kind command.
width 12
left 70 radius 90 rise -6 bank 12 kind tunnel
straight 90 rise -3 bank 0

# Named tunnel and bridge commands also apply to just their own segment.
tunnel 100 rise -4
straight 75 rise 2
bridge 100 rise 4
checkpoint

# Daylight corner and a long finishing run give time to straighten and brake.
right 15 radius 100 rise -1 bank -12
right 25 radius 100 rise -2
right 15 radius 100 rise -1 bank 0
straight 170 rise -8
finish
